From 1fe9628e5daeb210861b6eff5db29a39448f51e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:10:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 094/118] tls: spoof and spoof_method, the route options
 tls_spoof and tls_spoof_method (from sing-box 1.14)

A forged ClientHello with a name of the user's choice is sent before the real one, in
a way that makes the server drop it: an old sequence number, a wrong checksum, an old
acknowledgment, an MD5 signature option, an old timestamp. A middlebox that decides by
the first ClientHello of a connection sees the forged name.

The code is that of sing-box 1.14.2 (commits 40e2b5fd4, a33858523, d9290bc94,
704853b3b), Linux only: the TLS option of the outbound TLS clients, the option of the
route, route-options and bypass actions, the tests. The forged segment is encoded in the
package itself, since the packet headers of sing-tun are internal on this line; a test
holds its bytes, for every method and for IPv4 and IPv6, to those of 1.14.
